        "like": 3
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "There's no way VRChat can implement this request unless you specify what exactly you'd like to be changed.\n\"Lag compensation\" is such a broad term. And I think there's a *lot* of misinformation in this thread... 😫\nFor example, if I stab someone in Murder... What should happen? How should VRChat compensate for lag? What role should the master play? What tools are world creators missing? Why can't we compensate for lag ourselves?\nAs a world creator, I try to give the local user the benefit of the doubt, unless it's a competitive game. And it's been working OK so far. I'd like to have more control on how remote player movement is interpolated... Would you describe that as 'lag compensation'? Or should that be a different Canny?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
